 I'm here to help you get started with writing an SystemVerilog module for an Low-Density Parity-Check (LDPC) encoder for an FPGA implementation. Since the design and specifications might vary, I will provide you with a general outline of an LDPC encoder using the Syndrome-Based Parity Check (SynBPC) method. This method is well-suited for FPGA implementations due to its parallel nature.

```systemverilog
module ldpc_encoder (
    input logic vector [N-1:0] data_in, // N-bit input data
    output logic vector [K-1:0] parity_bits_out, // K-bit parity bits output
    parameter WIDTH = 8, // Bit width
    parameter N = 32, // Input data length
    parameter K = 8, // Number of parity bits
    parameter NNZ_PER_ROW = 4 // Non-zero elements per row
);

// Define the number of rows based on the number of non-zero elements per row and input data length
parameter P = ceil(N / (NNZ_PER_ROW * WIDTH));

// Declare internal signals and constants
logic vector [N-1:0][P-1:0] H; // Parity check matrix H
logic vector [N-1:0] syndrome; // Syndrome vector
logic vector [N-1:0] temp; // Temporary signal

// Initialize the parity check matrix H
initial begin
    $display("Initializing H matrix...");
    for (int i = 0; i < P; i = i + 1) begin
        for (int j = 0; j < N; j = j + WIDTH) begin
            if ((i * NNZ_PER_ROW + j / WIDTH) < NNZ_PER_ROW) begin
                H[i][j : j+WIDTH-1] = 1'b1;
            end else begin
                H[i][j : j+WIDTH-1] = 1'b0;
            end
        end
    end
end

