 I'd be happy to help you resolve the issue with your Wordpress blog post not having an image displayed when shared on Facebook. Here's a step-by-step guide to ensure that Facebook picks up the correct image for your post:

1. **Set a Featured Image:** The first thing you want to make sure of is that you have set a featured image for your blog post in WordPress. Go to your dashboard, find the post you want to share, and add or select a featured image in the "Featured Image" module. This image will be the one that Facebook uses by default when sharing the link.

2. **Check Open Graph Meta Tags:** Open Graph meta tags are HTML tags that provide additional information about the content on your webpage. These tags help social media platforms like Facebook understand what the content is about and how it should be displayed. Make sure your post has the necessary Open Graph meta tags. You can check this by using the Facebook Sharing Debugger tool (https://developers.facebook.com/tools/debug). Enter the URL of your blog post into the debugger, click "Debug," and look for the "Sharing Image" section. If there's no image being displayed, the debugger might suggest an alternative image based on its crawl. Try setting the featured image again and run the debugger until the correct image appears.

3. **Use a plugin:** If you don't want to manually add Open Graph meta tags every time you publish a new post, consider using a plugin such as Yoast SEO or All In One SEO Pack. These plugins allow you to easily set the featured image and Open Graph meta tags for each post directly from the WordPress editor.

