 I'd be happy to help you write a Google Apps Script that searches for a place name in a given column and stores its latitude and longitude in two other columns. Here's an example of how you can do this using the Google Maps Geocoding API:

```javascript
function searchPlacesAndLogCoordinates() {
  // Replace 'SheetName' with the name of your Google Spreadsheet sheet.
  const sheetName = "SheetName";
  const apiKey = "YOUR_API_KEY"; // Replace with your Google Maps Geocoding API key.

  // Get the active spreadsheet and sheet by name.
  const ss = SpreadsheetApp.getActiveSpreadsheet();
  const sheet = ss.getSheetByName(sheetName);

  // Define the column numbers where you want to store the address, latitude, and longitude.
  const addressColumn = 1;
  const latitudeColumn = 2;
  const longitudeColumn = 3;

  // Search for places and log their coordinates.
  for (let i = 2; i <= sheet.getLastRow(); i++) {
    const placeAddress = sheet.getRange(i, addressColumn).getValue();
    if (placeAddress) {
      const geocoder = Maps.newGeocoder();
      const location = geocoder.geocode(placeAddress);
      const lat = location[0].geometry.location.lat();
      const lng = location[0].geometry.location.lng();

      // Log the results in the respective columns.
      sheet.getRange(i, latitudeColumn).setValue(lat);
      sheet.getRange(i, longitudeColumn).setValue(lng);
    }
  }
}
```

