function smart_sort_array($set, $order = 'ASC') {
    // Check if the set is an array
    if (!is_array($set)) {
        throw new Exception('$set must be an array');
    }

    // Loop through the array and sort based on age
    for ($i = 0; $i < count($set) - 1; $i++) {
        for ($j = $i + 1; $j < count($set); $j++) {
            if (($order == 'DESC' && $set[$i]['age'] < $set[$j]['age']) || ($order == 'ASC' && $set[$i]['age'] > $set[$j]['age'])) {
                // Swap elements if condition is met
                $temp = $set[$i];
                $set[$i] = $set[$j];
                $set[$j] = $temp;
            }
        }
    }

    return $set;
}
```

This function takes an associative array `$set` as its first argument and an optional second argument `$order`, defaulting to 'ASC' for ascending order. The function checks that the input is valid before attempting to sort the array using a simple switching algorithm. The array is sorted based on the age key in each sub-array, in accordance with the specified order.

