Now, let's move on to your second question. Here is an example Java program code that calculates the duration between two dates while considering the time zones:
```java
import java.time.Instant;
import java.time.ZoneId;
import java.time.ZonedDateTime;
public class DateDurationCalculator {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String date1Str = "2022-01-01T10:00:00Z"; // Use ISO format with Z offset for UTC time
        String date2Str = "2022-01-01T15:30:00-05:00"; // Use ISO format with time zone offset
        ZonedDateTime date1 = ZonedDateTime.parse(date1Str);
        ZoneId zoneId1 = ZoneId.systemDefault(); // Assuming default time zone is UTC for this example
        Instant instant1 = date1.toInstant();
        ZonedDateTime date2 = ZonedDateTime.parse(date2Str).withZoneSameInstant(zoneId1);
        Instant instant2 = date2.toInstant();
        Duration duration = Duration.between(instant1, instant2);
        System.out.println("Duration: " + duration);
    }
}
```
